# Habitex AI: System Architecture, Topology, and Spatial Contract Design

## 1. Executive Architectural Overview & System Topology

Habitex AI decouples the high-frequency rendering loop of spatial computing runtimes (Apple Vision Pro visionOS / WebXR) from the asynchronous, multi-agent reasoning loops powered by the Google GenAI SDK (`@google/genai`), using Supabase as the low-latency state bus and persistence engine.

```
       +-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
       |                       SPATIAL CLIENT RUNTIMES (Edge Nodes)                       |
       |                                                                                   |
       |   +---------------------------------------+   +-------------------------------+   |
       |   |   Apple Vision Pro (visionOS Native)  |   |    WebXR Runtime (Browser)    |   |
       |   |   - ARKit / RealityKit                |   |    - Three.js / WebGPU        |   |
       |   |   - USDZ Scene Graph Engine           |   |    - WebXR Device API         |   |
       |   +-------------------+-------------------+   +---------------+---------------+   |
       +-----------------------|---------------------------------------|-------------------+
                               | HTTPS / WSS                           | HTTPS / WSS
                               | (Mutations, Scans, WebRTC Audio)      | (Mutations, Scans)
                               v                                       v
+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                     NEXT.JS APP ROUTER (BFF & INGRESS CONTROLLER)                       |
|                                                                                          |
|  +---------------------------+  +--------------------------+  +-----------------------+  |
|  |   Route Handlers (REST)   |  |   Server Actions / SSE   |  |  Edge Mesh Ingestion  |  |
|  |   - /api/spatial/scan     |  |   - Design Session Init  |  |  - Spatial Anchor Val |  |
|  |   - /api/spatial/mutate   |  |   - Dynamic Prompt Exec  |  |  - Decimation Pipe    |  |
|  +-------------+-------------+  +------------+-------------+  +-----------+-----------+  |
+----------------|-----------------------------|----------------------------|--------------+
                 |                             |                            |
                 | GenAI Tool Invocations      | Realtime Sync / DB I/O     | Blob Uploads
                 v                             v                            v
+--------------------------------+  +--------------------------------+  +------------------+
|   GOOGLE GENAI SDK ENGINE      |  |      SUPABASE PLATFORM         |  | SUPABASE STORAGE |
|                                |  |                                |  |                  |
|  +--------------------------+  |  |  +--------------------------+  |  | - Raw Meshes     |
|  |  gemini-3.7-flash        |  |  |  | PostgreSQL 16 (pgvector) |  |  |   (.ply, .usdz)  |
|  |  - Spatial Reasoning     |  |  |  | - Spatial Layout Tables  |  |  | - Optimized GLB  |
|  |  - Tool/Function Calling |  |  |  | - Catalog Embeddings     |  |  | - KTX2 Textures  |
|  +--------------------------+  |  |  +------------+-------------+  |  +------------------+
|  +--------------------------+  |  |               |                |
|  |  Multimodal Vision Pipe  |  |  |  +------------v-------------+  |
|  |  - PBR Texture Gen       |  |  |  | Supabase Realtime Engine |  |
|  |  - Lighting Extraction   |  |  |  | - Scene Graph Channel    |  |
|  +--------------------------+  |  |  | - Collaborative Broadcast|  |
|                                |  |  +--------------------------+  |
+--------------------------------+  +--------------------------------+
```

### Component Boundaries & Protocols

| Boundary / Link | Protocol | Payload Type | Latency Target | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Spatial Client $\leftrightarrow$ Next.js** | HTTPS / HTTP/2 | JSON / Multipart FormData | $< 120\text{ ms}$ | Ingestion of room scans, mesh manifests, camera telemetry, and prompt dispatch. |
| **Spatial Client $\leftrightarrow$ Supabase** | WSS (WebSocket) | JSON (Realtime Broadcast / CDC) | $< 40\text{ ms}$ | High-frequency dynamic scene graph synchronisation, transform updates, user presence. |
| **Next.js $\leftrightarrow$ Supabase DB** | Direct TCP (Pooler) | SQL / Parametric Queries | $< 10\text{ ms}$ | Asset catalog retrieval, spatial state transactions, pgvector similarity lookups. |
| **Next.js $\leftrightarrow$ Supabase Storage** | S3 API / HTTPS | Binary streams | Bandwidth Bound | Direct presigned uploads for Room Scans (.usdz/.ply) and PBR textures. |
| **Next.js $\leftrightarrow$ Google GenAI SDK** | HTTPS (TLS 1.3) | Proto/JSON (`@google/genai`) | Streamed ($< 800\text{ ms}$ TTFT) | Structured function calling, spatial reasoning, multimodal texture/lighting generation. |

---

## 2. Spatial Data Contracts: Habitex Spatial Schema (HSS v1.0)

All spatial systems require a deterministic, mathematically unified Coordinate Reference System (CRS). 

### Coordinate Conventions
* **Basis**: Right-Handed Cartesian Coordinate System ($+X = \text{Right}$, $+Y = \text{Up}$, $+Z = \text{BackwardsTowardsViewer}$).
* **Units**: SI Metres ($1.000 = 1.0\text{ m}$).
* **Origin ($[0,0,0]$)**: World reference point anchored to the primary floor plane centre established at the initialisation of the spatial scan.
* **Rotations**: Expressed in Hamilton Unit Quaternions: $q = [w, x, y, z]$, where $\|q\| = 1$.

```ts
/**
 * Habitex Spatial Schema v1.0 (HSS)
 * Foundational Geometric & Mathematical Primitives
 */

export type Vector3D = [x: number, y: number, z: number];
export type Quaternion = [w: number, x: number, y: number, z: number];
export type Matrix4x4 = [
  number, number, number, number,
  number, number, number, number,
  number, number, number, number,
  number, number, number, number
];

export interface BoundingBox3D {
  min: Vector3D;
  max: Vector3D;
  center: Vector3D;
  extents: Vector3D; // Half-dimensions [width/2, height/2, depth/2]
}

export interface Transform3D {
  position: Vector3D;
  rotation: Quaternion;
  scale: Vector3D;
  matrixWorld?: Matrix4x4;
}
```

### Physical Room Scan Ingestion Contract

Spatial devices extract geometry, structural semantic planes, and environment light probes via ARKit or WebXR Depth APIs. This payload is transmitted to the Next.js API ingress for processing and spatial reasoning.

```ts
export type StructuralPlaneType = 
  | 'floor'
  | 'ceiling'
  | 'wall'
  | 'door'
  | 'window'
  | 'table'
  | 'seat'
  | 'unknown';

export interface SpatialPlaneAnchor {
  id: string;
  semanticType: StructuralPlaneType;
  confidence: number; // 0.0 to 1.0
  transform: Transform3D;
  dimensions: [width: number, height: number]; // Dimensions in metres
  boundaryPolygon: Vector3D[]; // Planar perimeter vertices relative to anchor
  isPrimaryFloor?: boolean;
}

export interface EnvironmentalLightProbe {
  ambientIntensityLumens: number;
  colorTemperatureKelvin: number;
  sphericalHarmonicsCoefficients: number[]; // 27 floats (9 3-channel coefficients for L2 SH)
  dominantDirectionalLight?: {
    direction: Vector3D;
    color: [r: number, g: number, b: number];
    intensityLux: number;
  };
}

export interface PhysicalRoomScanManifest {
  scanId: string;
  userId: string;
  capturedAt: string; // ISO 8601
  clientRuntime: 'VisionOS' | 'WebXR';
  deviceHardware: string;
  rawMeshStorageKey?: string; // Reference to Supabase Storage (.ply or .usdz)
  bounds: BoundingBox3D;
  planes: SpatialPlaneAnchor[];
  lightProbe: EnvironmentalLightProbe;
  semanticOpenings: {
    doors: Array<{ id: string; transform: Transform3D; width: number; height: number }>;
    windows: Array<{ id: string; transform: Transform3D; width: number; height: number }>;
  };
}
```

### Dynamic Scene State Representation Contract

The authoritative scene graph managed between Supabase Realtime, the Next.js agent orchestrator, and spatial frontends.

```ts
export type SurfaceMaterialType = 'pbr_standard' | 'clearcoat' | 'sheen';

export interface PBRMaterialSpecification {
  materialId: string;
  name: string;
  albedoFactor: [r: number, g: number, b: number, a: number];
  roughnessFactor: number;
  metallicFactor: number;
  normalTextureUrl?: string;
  baseColorTextureUrl?: string;
  roughnessMetallicTextureUrl?: string;
  uvScale: [u: number, v: number];
}

export interface SpatialEntityInstance {
  instanceId: string;
  catalogItemId: string;
  sku: string;
  name: string;
  transform: Transform3D;
  boundingBox: BoundingBox3D;
  assetUris: {
    gltf: string;       // WebXR optimized format (Draco/KTX2)
    usdz: string;       // visionOS / RealityKit native format
  };
  materialOverrides: Record<string, PBRMaterialSpecification>; // targetMeshNode -> Material
  physics: {
    isStatic: boolean;
    massKg: number;
    collisionLayer: 'furniture' | 'decor' | 'obstacle';
  };
  commerce: {
    retailerId: string;
    unitPrice: number;
    currency: string;
    inStock: boolean;
  };
}

export interface SceneGraphState {
  version: number;
  sessionId: string;
  environmentLighting: {
    overrideEnabled: boolean;
    ambientLightColor: [r: number, g: number, b: number];
    ambientIntensity: number;
    directionalRig: Array<{
      id: string;
      position: Vector3D;
      direction: Vector3D;
      intensity: number;
      castShadows: boolean;
    }>;
  };
  wallSurfaceModifications: Array<{
    planeAnchorId: string;
    material: PBRMaterialSpecification;
  }>;
  floorSurfaceModifications: Array<{
    planeAnchorId: string;
    material: PBRMaterialSpecification;
  }>;
  entities: SpatialEntityInstance[];
}
```

