### Key Technical Patterns Enforced

1. **SDK Compliance**: Directly implements `@google/genai` using the `GoogleGenAI` constructor with `gemini-3.7-flash` and `text-embedding-004`. Deprecated SDKs (`@google/generative-ai`) and older model families are strictly avoided.
2. **Server-Sent Events (SSE) Execution Loop**: Handled via Edge/Node Web Streams (`TransformStream` + `Uint8Array` encoder). Emits explicit discrete events (`thought`, `tool_call`, `guardrail_check`, `scene_mutation`, `commentary`, `done`) enabling VisionOS and WebXR frontends to update 3D transforms before receiving the final text response.
3. **Deterministic Geometric Integrity**: Tool executions run through `SpatialGuardrailsEngine.validateEntityPlacement` implementing 3D Separating Axis Theorem (SAT) over Oriented Bounding Boxes (OBB). If collisions or boundary violations occur, actionable suggestions are returned to the agent loop for self-healing.
4. **Database Atomicity & Replication**: Mutations are bundled and committed via the PostgreSQL stored procedure `commit_spatial_mutation_tx` and broadcast instantly to connected spatial collaborators via Supabase Realtime CDC channels.

# Habitex AI: Spatial Computing Client Bridge & Scene Graph Synchronization

This architecture implements the client-side spatial runtime bridge connecting Next.js App Router with WebXR and Three.js/React Three Fiber (R3F), alongside support for Apple VisionOS.

